        "id": 6347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-03-21T16:08:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The issue with these is it\u0027s not a complete list:\nhttps://ietf-wg-acme.github.io/acme/#errors\n\nWe mainly did this for users to be able to do e.g.\n\n  err.Type \u003d\u003d acme.ErrMalformed\n\nAnother thing is Error.Type (which is what these are) is usually not enough to handle an error. You\u0027d normally need other Error fields. In fact, Marcin sadly hand to resort to something like this:\n\n  if err.Type \u003d\u003d acme.ErrMalformed \u0026\u0026 strings.Contains(err.Detail, \"already in use\") {\n    // handle a case where account key has already been used\n    // for registration\n  }",
